#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:110
#: 799963aa02c3476fba944b9e88f3f9c5
msgid "Connecting to SITL running in WSL on the same machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:111
#: da8826f45ebe41dd81cbece2333caca1
msgid "Depending on your PC's power and version of RealFlight, it may be possible to run SITL under WSL and connect to RealFlight for the graphics and physics modeling. In this case you open the WSL instance and start SITL:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:113
#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:142
#: 3aca2876a7af429684891ade1d4162dc
#: c950fd2452b44501a3fd06faf1c16db4
msgid "cd ArduCopter (See Note below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:114
#: 9da9fee707ee49aea8219412845226cd
msgid "for WSL1: type \"sim_vehicle.py -f flightaxis:127.0.0.1 -\\-map -\\-console\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:115
#: 5788e2af0b5e4a6188dfef4f814e196e
msgid "for WSL2: you will need to determine the gateway for the virtual machine by using the command ``route -n``, then using the gateway ip in the SITL startup command for flightaxis: \"sim_vehicle.py -f flightaxis:<gateway ip addr> -\\-map -\\-console\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:117
#: 55426aea7d2e41e5869b9c86265424e7
msgid "back on RealFlight push the red \"RESET\" button on the transmitter, or spacebar on PC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:118
#: 66d40dc6f60a417b80fedec9a4a423e4
msgid "after about a minute, the vehicle should be visible on the SITL map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:119
#: 590c44efdc17410c98e69bc68338bcc3
msgid "from within SITL type ``param load <filename>``  to load the parameter found in the same directory as the model. You may have to load them again, after typing ``param fetch``, in order to load parameters that require enabling before presenting their parameter set.  And, in some cases, you may even need to restart SITL in order for some new parameters, such as output function changes, to take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:121
#: ed7df35b58a64919ba1b08ce6de0c231
msgid "the above can be avoided if you add the parameter file during the start of SITL with the \"--add-param-file=*pathtofile* \"....ie: sim_vehicle.py -f flightaxis:x.x.x.x -\\-map -\\-console --add-param-file=*pathtofile* -w. This adds the param file as a default and then wipes any previous param changes that may exist in the simulation directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:123
#: f22ae05caedf4784a65396ccc7d80693
msgid "The performance of the connection can be checked, after connecting to SITL, by opening the \"NavGuides\" widget in Realflight. The \"Graphics Frames/Sec\" count should be over 200 for the vehicle physics and interactions with the simulation to be accurate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:125
#: c59e2c62b05c44c7989bae9b468c64ae
msgid "the above was for a Copter. Change the directory to ArduPlane or ArduRover for those types of vehicles before beginning sim_vehicle.py or add the -v <vehicle type> directive when starting it. You cannot use a host name for the the address of the windows machine, you must use an IP address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:128
#: b1c366f7655544b689723e1864797a68
msgid "Connecting to SITL running on a separate (or Virtual) machine:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:130
#: bbcb4ba255e44349a4e006e15c9beeb9
msgid "This technique spreads the processing requirements between two PCs: one Windows machine running RealFlight and the physics/flight graphics, and another Linux PC or Linux VM running the SITL models. It also allows you to test and use locally generated code, rather than only the master branch, used by Mission Planner SITL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:135
#: 5f297675743d4f4fbc134f6ba7f83bfd
msgid "best performance is obtained using a direct Gigabit Ethernet connection between machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:136
#: e973e3feaffa4c21b8b3ffe2d9740d89
msgid "determine the IP address of the Windows machine running RealFlight by opening a console and entering \"ipconfig\".The result will likely be something like 192.168.x.x OR 127.0.0.1 if running sitl on a Windows machine using :ref:`cygwin <building-setup-windows-cygwin>`, :ref:`Windows 11 WSL2 <building-setup-windows11>`, or :ref:`Windows 10 WSL <building-setup-windows10_new>`, or similar to 10.26.0.2 if using a direct ethernet connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:138
#: 0c800b6595fb4cbd993651b302237d0d
msgid "be sure that there is no firewall preventing communication between the PCs. You should be able to \"ping\" one from the other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:140
#: c3273cf18e0644cdb479db788d285acc
msgid "on the separate machine where SITL will run, start SITL sim_vehicle.py with \"-f flightaxis:192.168.x.x\" or if using a traditional helicopter, \"-f heli -\\-model flightaxis:192.168.x.x\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:143
#: 9c75bd7c0b854741b8b92f0a447237c2
msgid "sim_vehicle.py -f flightaxis:192.168.x.x -\\-map -\\-console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:144
#: 36ea50e4d19f43adacf784cd4b5f13e3
msgid "then follow the remaining commands as in the :ref:`SITL under WSL <sitl-on-wsl>` section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:148
#: 3ab829595c184cb9845669f7b3b3d6e1
msgid "Using ready-made models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:150
#: 21059cf1a6c04be495f79a4b2109ee74
msgid "As mentioned above, RealFlight allows designing your own custom vehicles including choosing the size, weight, appearance, and motor and control surface placement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:152
#: ef8337f4a9914e5aad277752019446c2
msgid "A number of custom models have been created by ArduPilot developers and stored in the `ArduPilot/SITL_Models repository <https://github.com/ArduPilot/SITL_Models>`__. You should be able to :ref:`clone <git-clone>` this repo using ``git clone https://github.com/ArduPilot/SITL_Models.git`` and then load the models into RealFlight. In the directory for each model there is a .parm file that can be loaded into SITL so that appropriate tunings parameters are set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:156
#: 25fa2dfca9064e719f448dd22a9f5469
msgid "The SITL_Models folder has a RealFlight directory with a WIP sub-directory for models in progress, and a Released_Models directory, which have models that have been tested to work with the InterLink controllers and have README.md files describing their setup and special features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:158
#: d74fa1b5f77b4c2eae29c153f464204f
msgid "To import one of these models:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:160
#: a06f2b776f8b42e08bcc97bd7026f7a1
msgid "on RealFlight select Simulation >> Import >> RealFlight Archive (RFX, G3X) and select the model you're interested in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:161
#: 3ec03b51d0bf406c8ab21540fa1c2ce0
msgid "select Aircraft >> Select Aircraft and select the model imported from the above step"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:167
#: 2ea0ace0980b4de3909744d8733c0474
msgid "from within SITL type ``param load <filename>``  to load the parameter found in the same directory as the model, as in the above example. You may have to load them again, after typing ``param fetch``, in order to load parameters that require enabling before presenting their parameter set.  And in some cases you may need to restart SITL in order for some parameters to take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:174
#: 8a0bf757af4c4af186f38f7690580569
msgid "OpenTX use with RealFlight and SITL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:176
#: ae2d2d23fe834a099596f14ac4a0c1ec
msgid "There are three approaches you can use. Minimal: which only setups up the AETR flight control axes, and Maximal: Which gets at least 7 channels to the SITL module, more closely emulating how you would really use the TX to fly the vehicle, and Interlink DX controller emulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:178
#: 59ca373d88a54677bf32098a407dbe27
msgid "Minimal: power up the TX, program a new plane model for use with the sim with the wizard, plug in USB, select joystick (later OpenTX versions allow permanent selection in the main radio setup page). Select Simulation-> Select controller in RealFlight. Select Taranis, and proceed to setup the aileron,elevator,rudder, and throttle and calibrate them. Now to change modes or set switches, you will need to use MAVProxy or Mission Planner commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:180
#: fa0152e02bf946d9a2767d47b1163f3f
msgid "Maximal: In addition to the above, setup the TX model with switches or sliders/pots for channels 5,6,7, and 8. Then add them for functions in the RealFlight controller setup. Do not be concerned about the function names, we just want them to be passed thru to the SITL model. Now you can assign ``RCx_OPTION`` functions to those channels in the model parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:182
#: f1cc6ba4227948a68f617033455a58b5
msgid "InterLink DX/Elite controller emulation: This closely mimics these Interlink  controllers, normally sold with RealFlight. This allows the use of a transmitter with normal RealFlight simulations as well as SITL which closely matches the physical layout of the Interlink controllers. See :ref:`interlink-emulation` for setup details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:184
#: 4b6871b130324b71a565bd2fc8bd06b6
msgid "To setup a six position mode switch, you would do so just as explained :ref:`here<common-rc-transmitter-flight-mode-configuration>` for an OpenTX transmitter, but first calibrate the RealFlight  controller using a dual position switch on the mode channel. Then change the transmitter back to provide the six PWM levels. This required since RealFlight auto-scales from the calibration values, so if your six PWM levels are centered in the recognition ranges , then the channel's PWM extremes will not be used for calibration and the PWM levels will be altered by RealFlight before passing on to the SITL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:193
#: a2c9de807ea848228f0b674e4ad186a8
msgid "Creating a RealFlight Model for Simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-realflight.rst:195
#: ea5a5b0a2a014daaa49c646955849c07
msgid "See `this blog post <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/creating-a-realflight-model-with-blender>`__ for details on creating a RF model for flightaxis simulation."
msgstr ""
